<title>JAPAN: Argentina launches 50 bln yen 6.0% Euroyen--Nikko.</title>
<headline>Argentina launches 50 bln yen 6.0% Euroyen--Nikko.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina launched 50 billion yen worth of 6.0 percent Euroyen bonds on Thursday, Nikko Securities said.</p>
<p>The bonds are due on March 24, 2005. They are priced at 99.00 and are lead-managed by Nikko Europe, a subsidiary of Nikko Securities.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the terms:</p>
<p>AMT 50 bln yen</p>
<p>COUPON 6.0%</p>
<p>TYPE Euroyen</p>
<p>ISS PRICE 99.00</p>
<p>MATURITY March 24, 2005</p>
<p>PAY DATE Nov 12,1996</p>
<p>LAST RATING B1 (Moody's), BB- (S&amp;P)</p>
<p>LEAD MANAGER Nikko Europe</p>
</text>
